heet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"pkPaymentError(forStripeError:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay\/stripecore\/stpapiclient\/pkpaymenterror(forstripeerror:)"},"doc://com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay/documentation/StripeApplePay/StripeCore":{"url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay\/stripecore","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay\/documentation\/StripeApplePay\/StripeCore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"StripeCore","abstract":[],"role":"collection"}}}